\section{Moduli stacks in $p$-adic Hodge theory}

In this section, we construct a symplectic variant of the moduli stacks of \'etale $\pgma$-modules constructed in [ref] and prove its properties including the existence of closed substacks parameterizing potentially crystalline representations. We also construct symplectic variants for the $p$-adic formal algebraic stacks considered in [ref], namely, the moduli stacks of Breuil--Kisin modules, and \'etale $\phi$-modules. Then we study the geometric properties of potentially crystalline substacks using local models in \S[•].

### Symplectic \'etale $\pgma$-modules

Only in this subsection, we allow $K/\Qp$ to be ramified.

For a $p$-adically complete $\cO$-algebra $R$, we write $\cX_n(R)$ for the groupoid of projective \'etale $\pgma$-modules of rank $n$ with $R$-coefficients, in the sense of [ref]. Then $\cX_n$ is a Noetherian formal algebraic stack over $\spf \cO$ (Corollary 5.5.17 in loc.~cit.). When $R$ is a finite $\cO$-algebra, there is an equivalence of categories between the category of projective \'etale $(\varphi,\Gamma)$-modules with $R$-coefficients and the category of continuous representations of $G_K$ on finite projective $R$-modules. The goal of this subsection is to construct a moduli stack of symplectic $\pgma$-modules over $\cO$ using the Emerton--Gee stack.

We start by defining a symplectic variant of \'etale $\pgma$-modules.

**Defn.** 
Let $R$ be a $p$-adically complete $\cO$-algebra. A symplectic projective \'etale $\pgma$-module (of rank 4) with $R$-coefficients is a triple $(M,N,\al)$ where $M\in \cX_4(R)$, $N\in \cX_1(R)$, and $\al: M \simeq M^\vee \otimes N$ is an isomorphism between rank 4 \'etale $\pgma$-modules satisfying the alternating condition $(\al^\vee\otimes N)^\mo \circ \al=-1_{M}$. Note that $\al$ induces a non-degenerate bilinear pairing
$$
 p_\al: M\times M &\ra N
