 (m_1, m_2) &\mapsto \al(m_1)(m_2)
$$
that is alternating, i.e.~$p_\al(m_1,m_2) = -p_\al(m_2,m_1)$. Then a morphism $F: (M,N,\al) \ra (M',N',\al')$ of symplectic projective \'etale $\pgma$-modules is a pair of morphisms $f:M\ra M'$ and $g:N\ra N'$ of \'etale $\pgma$-modules that commutes with the bilinear pairings induced by $\al$ and $\al'$. 
We write $\cX_\Sym(R)$ for the groupoid of projective symplectic \'etale $\pgma$-modules with $R$-coefficients.

